# Debugging this engine

Read `debug-notes.md` before diagnosing Octane, math, parse, or GC crashes.

- Compare only against `../mquickjs` (C). Do not search other workspace dirs.
- Build `-Doptimize=ReleaseFast`. Do not iterate with full `zig build octane`.
- Fix one correctness bug, then stop. Performance last.
- Several Octane failures were `libm_lib.zig` UB / precedence / signedness.
- Isolated suite repros are not enough; need heap pressure from earlier Octane files/suites.
- `mqjs tests/octane/run.js <suite>` segfaults in host argv (Zig slices as `char**`). Not the engine bug.
- Typescript flake: unique-string insert used a stale index after `js_is_numeric_string` GC. Do not revert.
- C `JS_POP_VALUE` assigns the GC-updated pointer back. Do not discard `popValue` when the local is used after (CodeLoad, `label_name`, `js_create_property` `prop`, ToPrimitive `method`, bound `params`).
- Unique-string table is weak. C compact scans `arr->size` (restored). Do not re-scan only `unique_strings_len`. Do not re-add MakeUniqueString post-resize `find_atom` or `[len, cap)` UNDEFINED fill. Do not change `js_resize_value_array` copy size for all arrays.
